⭐ 1. What is Amazon S3?

Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is a fully managed object storage service by AWS.

👉 EC2 = compute
👉 RDS = database
👉 S3 = store any amount of unstructured data (objects)

S3 stores files as objects inside buckets, not as files inside folders like Linux/Windows.

⭐ 2. Why S3 is used?
🔥 Key Reasons to Use S3
Feature	Explanation
Unlimited Storage	Store unlimited objects.
Durability: 99.999999999% (11 9’s)	Data almost never gets lost.
Scalability	Auto scales without configs.
Security	IAM, Bucket Policies, ACL, MFA Delete.
Cross-region replication	Automatic multi-region copy.
Event Notifications	Trigger Lambda when file uploaded.
Lifecycle Policies	Auto move to Glacier cheap storage.
Low-cost	Only pay for what you store.
⭐ 3. How S3 Stores Data (Object Storage Explained)

Each uploaded file = Object

Every object contains:

Object Data

Metadata (content-type, size, last-modified)

Object Key (full path)

Version ID

Access Control info

S3 = Key-Value store
Key = File Path
Value = File + Metadata

Example:

bucket/photos/2025/profile.jpg


Key = photos/2025/profile.jpg

⭐ 4. S3 Bucket – What is it?

Bucket = Top-level container
You must create bucket first → then upload objects.

Bucket properties:

must be unique globally

choose region

enable public access or keep private

versioning, lifecycle rules, replication apply on bucket

⭐ 5. S3 is Global but Buckets are Regional

👉 S3 service is global
👉 Bucket physically exists in 1 region

Example:

Bucket: myshop-data

Region: ap-south-1 (Mumbai)
→ All files stored inside Mumbai data centers

⭐ 6. S3 Use Cases (Real Industry Uses)
Use Case	Explanation
Website hosting	Host static HTML website.
Backup & Restore	Store snapshots, logs, backups.
Data lake	Big data analytics, Athena, Redshift.
