⭐ 8. S3 Disadvantages
Disadvantage	Explanation
Not a filesystem	You cannot install apps like on EBS.
Eventual consistency (some features)	Not instant like database.
High retrieval cost for Glacier	Glacier is cheap but slow.
Cannot run OS / database	Only object storage.
⭐ 9. How S3 Pricing Works (Very Important)

S3 Cost depends on:

Storage (GB per month)

PUT, GET, DELETE requests

Data transfer

Replication

Lifecycle transitions

Accelerated transfer

CloudFront caching reduces S3 cost

FREE TIER:

5 GB Standard Storage

20,000 GET

2,000 PUT

⭐ 10. S3 Security Model (Hero Topic)

S3 security depends on 4 main access methods:

🔐 1. IAM Policies

Give user permission → list bucket, upload, delete.

🔐 2. Bucket Policies

Public access for website hosting, or cross-account access.

🔐 3. ACL (Legacy)

Object-level permissions (rarely used now).

🔐 4. Public Access Block

AWS blocks public access by default.

⭐ 11. S3 Data Consistency

Read-after-Write consistency for new objects

Strong consistency for overwrite & delete (updated by AWS in 2020)

⭐ 12. S3 Reliability — 11 9’s is how?

AWS stores multiple copies across multiple availability zones.

Even if:

1 data center burns

1 AZ fails

1 server crashes

Your data is still safe.

⭐ 13. S3 vs EBS vs EFS (Interview)
Feature	S3	EBS	EFS
Type	Object storage	Block storage	NFS file system
Mount to EC2	❌ No	✔ Yes	✔ Yes (multi EC2)
Use case	Images, backups, static files	OS disk, DB disk	Shared file storage
Price	Cheapest	Medium	Expensive
⭐ 14. S3 Limitations (Common Interview Q)

Max object size = 5TB

Max single upload = 5GB (multipart required above this)

100 buckets per account (can increase)

No partial update (object overwrite only)
